   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Optional Lab: Cost Function - Healthcare Accessibility\n",
    "\n",
    "<figure>\n",
    "    <center> <img src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1559757148-5e995136c87b\" style=\"width:1000px;height:200px;\" ></center>\n",
    "</figure>\n",
    "\n",
    "**Real-World Impact**: Millions of people worldwide struggle with high medical costs. Governments and insurers use models like this to predict costs, allocate resources, and design affordable healthcare systems — directly affecting quality of life and life expectancy."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Goals\n",
    "- Master the **cost function** $J(w,b)$\n",
    "- Apply it to **Healthcare Cost Prediction**\n",
    "- Understand how minimizing cost leads to better public health policy\n",
    "- Connect math to saving lives and reducing financial burden on families"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Tools"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "from sklearn.linear_model import LinearRegression\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import mean_squared_error, r2_score\n",
    "plt.style.use('seaborn-v0_8')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Problem Statement\n",
    "\n",
    "Predict annual healthcare costs based on average age of population (or individual age).\n",
    "\n",
    "| Average Age | Annual Healthcare Cost per Person ($1000s) |\n",
    "|-------------|-------------------------------------------|\n",
    "| 35          | 4.2                                       |\n",
    "| 45          | 6.8                                       |\n",
    "| 55          | 9.5                                       |\n",
    "| 65          | 13.2                                      |\n",
    "| 75          | 18.0                                      |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "x_train = np.array([35, 45, 55, 65, 75])\n",
    "y_train = np.array([4.2, 6.8, 9.5, 13.2, 18.0])\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Age:\", x_train)\n",
    "print(\"Cost ($1000s):\", y_train)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Cost Function Implementation"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def compute_cost(x, y, w, b): \n",
    "    m = x.shape[0]\n",
    "    cost_sum = 0 \n",
    "    for i in range(m): \n",
    "        f_wb = w * x[i] + b\n",
    "        cost = (f_wb - y[i]) ** 2\n",
    "        cost_sum += cost\n",
    "    return (1 / (2 * m)) * cost_sum"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Experiment\n",
    "w = 0.3\n",
    "b = -6.0\n",
    "cost = compute_cost(x_train, y_train, w, b)\n",
    "print(f\"w = {w}, b = {b} → Cost = {cost:.4f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Visualization"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def plot_health_model(w, b):\n",
    "    x_line = np.linspace(30, 80, 100)\n",
    "    y_pred = w * x_line + b\n",
    "    \n",
    "    plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
    "    plt.scatter(x_train, y_train, marker='o', c='red', s=80, label='Real Data')\n",
    "    plt.plot(x_line, y_pred, c='blue', linewidth=3, label=f'Model (w={w:.3f})')\n",
    "    plt.title('Age vs Healthcare Cost Prediction')\n",
    "    plt.xlabel('Average Age')\n",
    "    plt.ylabel('Annual Cost per Person ($1000s)')\n",
    "    plt.legend()\n",
    "    plt.grid(True)\n",
    "    plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "plot_health_model(0.3, -6.0)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Optimal Model with scikit-learn"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "X = x_train.reshape(-1, 1)\n",
    "model = LinearRegression()\n",
    "model.fit(X, y_train)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Best slope w     : {model.coef_[0]:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Best intercept b : {model.intercept_:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Minimum Cost     : {mean_squared_error(y_train, model.predict(X)):.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"R² Score         : {r2_score(y_train, model.predict(X)):.4f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "plot_health_model(model.coef_[0], model.intercept_)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Real-World Interpretation & Impact\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Slope (`w`)**: Each additional year of average age increases healthcare cost by ~`$w` thousand per person.\n",
    "- **Low Cost Model** → Accurate budget forecasting → Better insurance policies and public health funding.\n",
    "- **Policy Use**: Helps governments decide how much to invest in preventive care to flatten the cost curve.\n",
    "\n",
    "**This model directly influences**:\n",
    "- Medicare / Medicaid budgeting\n",
    "- Insurance premium setting\n",
    "- Resource allocation in aging societies"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Key Takeaways\n",
    "- Cost function = Measure of model error\n",
    - Minimizing it = Finding the most useful parameters\n",
    "- In healthcare, small improvements in prediction accuracy can save **billions** and improve millions of lives"
   ]
  }
 ],
